    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d892">

                <pb facs="1403" n="1389" xml:id="pg1389"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 EW/10–1344</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        British Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Halifax</hi>)</head>
                <p>The Secretary of State presents his compliments to His Excellency the British
                    Ambassador and has the honor to acknowledge the receipt of his note no. 628 of
                    October 13, 1944 (Ref. 150/27/44) in which it is stated that Sir Noel Charles
                    laid the problem of German war crimes against Italians before the Advisory
                    Council for Italy on October 6, 1944.</p>
                <p>The Department had in fact been informed to this effect by Mr. Kirk who stated
                    that the other representatives on the Council had been invited by Sir Noel
                    Charles to ascertain the views of their governments so that the matter of war
                    crimes both against and by Italians could be discussed by the Council at its
                    meeting on October 20, 1944. As stated in the Department’s memoranda of October
                    17, 1944, Mr. Kirk has been informed that the Department and the War and Navy
                    Departments concur in the suggestions put forward in the British Embassy’s <hi
                        rendition="#italic">aide-mémoires</hi> of October 3, 1944.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1944-10-26">October 26,
                            1944</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
